5\"><\/gap><\/p>"],"globalTypesConfigs":[{"type":"gap","widthMode":"asLongestWord","longestAlternativeSolutions":false,"ignoreCaseSensitivity":false}],"staticText":{"text":"<p><b>Figure it out<\/b><\/p><ul><li>My best friend and I are different!<\/li><li>I wake up every morning at 6.30. She wakes up late, at 8.<\/li><li>I have a big breakfast. She doesn\u2019t have breakfast.<\/li><li>I get to school at 7.45. She gets to school late.<\/li><\/ul>","backgroundColor":"lightgray","isSet":true}},{"instruction":{"english":"","german":"<p>Complete the rules in the grammar box.<\/p>"},"parts":["<p><b>Grammar | Present simple affirmative and negative<\/b><\/p><p>We use the present simple to talk about routines.<\/p><p>\u2022 To form the present simple affirmative, use the infinitive without to for <sup>1<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_7\"><\/gap>, <em>you, we, they<\/em>.<\/p><p>After <em>he, she, it<\/em>, add <sup>2<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_6\"><\/gap> to the infinitive.<\/p><p>\u2022 To form the present simple negative, use <\/p><p><sup>3<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_8\"><\/gap> after <em>I, you, we, they<\/em> and<\/p><p><sup>4<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_9\"><\/gap> after <em>he, she, it<\/em>.<\/p>"],"configs":[{"correctAnswer":"s","additionalAnswers":[{"answer":"-s"}],"id":"gap_6","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_1\/p12_ex1ab\/"},{"correctAnswer":"I","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_7","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_1\/p12_ex1ab\/"},{"correctAnswer":"don't","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_8","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_1\/p12_ex1ab\/"},{"correctAnswer":"doesn't","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_9","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_1\/p12_ex1ab\/"}],"staticConfigs":[],"globalTypesConfigs":[{"type":"gap","widthMode":"asLongestWord","lon